{"id": "core-s-churn", "name": "s_churn (Karras churn)", "family": "noise", "subfamily": "churn", "plain": "Before evaluating the model, raises the noise level a bit by adding fresh noise, then integrates from the raised level. A simple form of noise injection on non-ancestral solvers. In ComfyUI it is 0 by default on KSampler.", "math": "\u03b3 = min(s_churn/(N), \u221a2\u22121) if s_tmin \u2264 \u03c3_i \u2264 s_tmax else 0, N = len(sigmas)\u22121.\n\u03c3\u0302 = \u03c3_i(1+\u03b3). x \u2190 x + \u03b5\u00b7s_noise\u00b7\u221a(\u03c3\u0302\u00b2\u2212\u03c3_i\u00b2).\nThen x \u2190 x + d(x,\u03c3\u0302)\u00b7(\u03c3_{i+1}\u2212\u03c3\u0302).", "props": {"distribution": "standard normal", "spectrum": "white", "when_applied": "per-step", "normalizes_variance": "no"}, "evidence": [{"where": "ComfyUI/comfy/k_diffusion/sampling.py:190", "symbol": "sample_euler"}, {"where": "ComfyUI/comfy/k_diffusion/sampling.py:196", "symbol": "s_churn"}, {"where": "ComfyUI/comfy/k_diffusion/sampling.py:201", "symbol": "torch.randn_like"}, {"where": "ComfyUI/comfy/k_diffusion/sampling.py:269", "symbol": "sample_heun"}, {"where": "ComfyUI/comfy/k_diffusion/sampling.py:304", "symbol": "sample_dpm_2"}, {"where": "ComfyUI/comfy/k_diffusion/sampling.py:1117", "symbol": "sample_heunpp2"}], "providers": [{"pack": "core", "author": "Comfy Org and contributors", "licence": "GPL-3.0", "kind": "original", "nodes": [], "note": "", "verdict": "", "risks": [], "res4lyf": false}], "providers_n": 1, "in_core": true, "live": false, "needs_pack": false, "core_ref": {"sampler_name": "euler"}, "family_fit": [], "claims": [], "label": "from code", "surprise": "Churn draws torch.randn_like and ignores the sampler's noise_sampler, so sonar or PNS noise never reaches it and the global RNG sets it.", "rendered": true, "rendered_ids": ["flow-euler-beta", "flow-euler-karras", "flow-euler-kl_optimal", "flow-euler-simple", "sampler-euler"], "risks": [], "flagged_providers": 0, "licences": ["GPL-3.0"], "verdicts":